  "corrigendum_note": "2026-08-09 (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6242/6243 correction): the original per_game_results rows for sk48/ls20/cd82's 'think' arm (induction_ok=False, induction_failure_detail citing RemoteDisconnected) were llama-server crashes -- the server's own stderr log shows two SIGINTs back-to-back mid-generation, zero OOM/CUDA-error/abort, steady ~29.6 tok/s decode right up to death. That is this project's pre-existing, long-standing 'reaper' issue (ops/known-issues.md), NOT a think-mode capability signal -- NOT deleted or overwritten (Test-Run Record Integrity Discipline), preserved in place. Three NEW rows for the SAME (game, 'think') pairs were appended below (rerun_of_infra_crash=true,rerun_timestamp set), collected 2026-08-09 with carnot-conductor.service and carnot-orphan-cleanup.timer both STOPPED as an isolation test (see ops/known-issues.md for the isolation-test finding: 3/3 clean vs 4/4 crashed while those units were running, small-n, not fully conclusive). All three succeeded on the FIRST attempt with real reasoning engaged and real completions (16-20k chars), landing at heldout_accuracy=0.0 -- a genuine floor TIE with no_think on all three games, not the 'think fails outright' asymmetry the crash-corrupted reads implied. comparison_summary was recomputed via _summarize_pair() over the corrected row set (it naturally prefers the successful new rows: the filter is induction_ok truthy, and the original crashed rows have induction_ok=False, so they never entered the by-arm dicts to begin with -- no manual de-duplication needed). The admission-rate SIGN TEST result itself (scripts/analyze_exp6221_admission_rate.py) is UNCHANGED by this correction: 0.0 does not cross the 1.0 admission bar either way, so these three games were already correctly classified as ties for that specific metric; what changes is that they are now a CONFIRMED tie rather than an unmeasured crash. REQ-ARC-WMTE-6243's motivating 'mirror failure' claim (think fails outright on cd82/ls20/sk48, mirroring sp80's no_think failure) is RETRACTED -- sp80 remains the only genuine total-induction-failure case in this corpus."
